## 643. Maximum Average Subarray I

## Approach — Sliding Window
--  Find the sum of the first k elements.
--  This gives us the sum of the first subarray/window of size k.
--  Consider this sum as the current maximum sum.
--  Slide the window one position at a time.
--  Remove the element that is leaving the window: nums[i-k]
--  Add the new element entering the window: nums[i]
--  Compare the new window sum with the maximum sum and keep the larger one.
--  After checking all possible windows, divide the maximum sum by k to get the maximum average.

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public double findMaxAverage(int[] nums, int k) {
        int sum = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {
            sum += nums[i];
        }

